      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50366117",
      "snippet": "I&#x27;m curious how people on HN are using AI day to day, and came up with a list of questions I thought could be interesting to know. No need to answer every question of course, just wanted to get a gut feel how people are using AI.<p>1) What AI subscriptions are you personally paying for? (Claude, ChatGPT&#x2F;Codex, Cursor, etc)<p>- Which tiers?<p>- Have you purchased multiple subscriptions from the same provider (eg two Claude accounts)?<p>2) Are you using models outside (or instead) of those subscriptions? For example, pay-as-you-go APIs, OpenRouter, or locally hosted models.<p>- Which models and providers?<p>3) What coding harnesses and interfaces are you using? Are you sticking with the default CLIs or IDE integrations, or using alternatives like OpenCode, Pi, Aider, Muse Code, or custom-built harnesses?<p>- What made you switch harnesses (if you switched)?<p>4) Are you using any",
